  "location": "CAP30.23(4) vs CRR Art 72j(1)",
  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "CRR: CAP30.23(4) vs CRR Art 72j(1)",
      "summary": "Article 72j(1) CRR permits no deduction at exactly 5%, whereas Basel Framework CAP30.23(4) requires holdings to be less than 5%. The CRR does not provide discretion over this boundary.",
      "impact": "Position: G-SIB/G-SII, CET1 1000, designated trading-book holdings of other G-SIBs' TLAC instruments, aggregate exactly 50 (5.0%) Reading a: Basel CAP30.23(4): 50 is not less than 5% — condition fails, deduction 50 from Tier 2 Reading b: CRR Art 72j(1): 50 is equal to 5% — not deducted (0) Difference: Tier 2 deduction 50",
      "correction": "Confirm whether the boundary at exactly 5% in Article 72j(1) is intended."
    }
  },
